1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:08,570
DIMNA: Kalila, you would never open your mouth up in the sky, right? But 1 flying tortoise did, and almost lost everything!

2
00:00:08,720 --> 00:00:12,120
KALILA: A flying tortoise? Tortoises can't fly!

3
00:00:12,270 --> 00:00:16,120
DIMNA: This one did, with two kind ducks, and one little stick. Listen!

4
00:00:21,070 --> 00:00:27,580
Once upon a time, by a little green pond, there lived a tortoise and two ducks. They were the best of friends.

5
00:00:28,030 --> 00:00:32,450
The tortoise was kind, but he loved to talk. He talked all day long!

6
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:38,890
TORTOISE: Good morning, ducks! Did you see the sun? Did you see that bee? Did you see my new flower? Did you...

7
00:00:39,340 --> 00:00:41,790
DUCK: Yes, yes, dear friend. We saw everything!

8
00:00:42,790 --> 00:00:48,940
But one summer, the sun was very hot, and no rain came. Day by day, the little pond dried up.

9
00:00:49,390 --> 00:00:52,050
LITTLE DUCK: Oh no! Our pond is almost gone!

10
00:00:52,400 --> 00:00:55,480
DUCK: We must fly to the big blue lake, far away, over the hills.

11
00:00:55,930 --> 00:01:00,330
TORTOISE: Fly? But I cannot fly! Please don't leave me here alone!

12
00:01:00,780 --> 00:01:04,030
LITTLE DUCK: We will never leave you, friend. Let us think.

13
00:01:05,030 --> 00:01:09,630
DUCK: I have an idea! We will hold a stick, one end each. You bite the middle, and hold on tight!

14
00:01:10,080 --> 00:01:16,040
LITTLE DUCK: But remember: do not open your mouth. Not one word, until we land!

15
00:01:16,490 --> 00:01:21,480
TORTOISE: Not one word? Easy! I promise! I will be as quiet as a stone!

16
00:01:22,280 --> 00:01:27,410
So the tortoise bit the stick. The ducks flapped their wings, and up, up, up they flew!

17
00:01:27,860 --> 00:01:34,630
The tortoise saw the trees, the hills, and the clouds. Oh, how he wanted to talk! But he kept his mouth shut.

18
00:01:36,430 --> 00:01:41,450
Then they flew over a little village. The children looked up, and they pointed and laughed.

19
00:01:41,900 --> 00:01:43,860
GIRL: Look! Look! Two ducks are carrying a tortoise!

20
00:01:44,110 --> 00:01:45,970
BOY: Ha ha! What a silly tortoise!

21
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:51,140
The tortoise got very cross. Silly? Me? He wanted to answer so much!

22
00:01:51,590 --> 00:01:53,150
DUCK: Mm! Mm-mm!

23
00:01:53,600 --> 00:01:56,340
TORTOISE: I am not silly! I am...

24
00:01:56,840 --> 00:02:02,800
Oh no! He opened his mouth, and he let go of the stick! Down, down, down fell the tortoise...

25
00:02:03,150 --> 00:02:06,020
...right into a big, soft pile of hay! Flump!

26
00:02:06,570 --> 00:02:09,070
LITTLE DUCK: Friend! Friend! Are you all right?

27
00:02:11,070 --> 00:02:16,010
TORTOISE: I'm all right. My shell is strong. But, oh, I should have kept my mouth shut.

28
00:02:16,560 --> 00:02:19,010
DUCK: Next time, friend: think first, then speak!

29
00:02:20,410 --> 00:02:26,880
So the three friends walked the rest of the way together, slowly, slowly, all the way to the big blue lake.

30
00:02:27,430 --> 00:02:29,920
TORTOISE: Mm-hmm! Mm-hmm!

31
00:02:30,470 --> 00:02:34,380
And this time, the tortoise thought very carefully before every word.

32
00:02:36,780 --> 00:02:42,740
KALILA: So the tortoise could fly, but he could not wait. One word too early, and down he went!

33
00:02:42,890 --> 00:02:45,690
DIMNA: Think before you speak! Your words can wait a little.

34
00:02:46,240 --> 00:02:53,030
DIMNA: Persian word of the day! In Persian, a tortoise is laak-posht. Laak-posht! It means, a shell on the back!

35
00:02:53,180 --> 00:02:58,590
KALILA: Laak-posht. A tortoise. And a strong laak saved our little friend today.

36
00:03:00,140 --> 00:03:05,290
KALILA: And next time: three fish in a pond, and only one of them makes a plan.

